      "writtenOn": "2026-09-18T10:00:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Good question - it doesn\u0027t. \n\nRSV\u0027s client only speaks HTTP/1.1, so it never exercises onRequestRecv()/afterCompleteRequest() (the HTTP/2 stream-completion path in http2_connection.hpp). I tested that path separately with `curl --http2`, confirmed ALPN negotiated h2 and got a real HTTP/2 200, and verified via journalctl that both \"onRequestRecv streamId:1\" and \"res.completeRequestHandler called\" fired for that stream. \n\nAdded this detail to the commit message.",
